From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ship the vendored grammar licences in the wheel

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [upstream's wheels download the grammars at runtime and link none of them, so the gap only exists in a TSLP_LANGUAGES build]

The riscv64 wheel is built with TSLP_LANGUAGES=all, so _native.abi3.so is
371 third-party grammar repositories compiled into one shared library. Each
carries its own MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD or ISC licence whose binary
redistribution clause requires the copyright notice to travel with the
binary, and the wheel ships only tree-sitter-language-pack's own LICENSE.

project.license-files is an explicit PEP 639 list, so there is no default
glob to extend and the grammar licences have to be named. The build stages
them under packages/python/grammar-licenses/<language>/ from each grammar's
pinned revision; 357 of the 371 grammars publish a licence file there, and
the remaining 14 (brightscript, cooklang, corn, ebnf, eds, eex, elsa,
facility, groovy, move, pgn, slint, t32, vb) publish none at the revision
sources/language_definitions.json pins.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 packages/python/pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/python/pyproject.toml b/packages/python/pyproject.toml
index 1c56c19..a728f46 100644
--- a/packages/python/pyproject.toml
+++ b/packages/python/pyproject.toml
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ version = "1.15.8"
 description = "Pre-compiled tree-sitter grammars for 371 programming languages"
 keywords = [ "language-pack", "parser", "syntax", "tree-sitter" ]
 license = "MIT"
-license-files = [ "LICENSE" ]
+license-files = [ "LICENSE", "grammar-licenses/*/*" ]
 authors = [ { name = "Na'aman Hirschfeld" } ]
 requires-python = ">=3.10"
 classifiers = [
